1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:09,093
Most AI history tools sound sure of themselves, and you cannot tell what is real. So I built a radio station that is not allowed to guess.

2
00:00:09,643 --> 00:00:19,014
This is Ghost Town Radio. The town is Bodie, California, in eighteen seventy-nine and eighty. Every word comes from public domain newspapers.

3
00:00:19,564 --> 00:00:23,530
Turn the dial to pick an hour. It works by touch, mouse, or keyboard.

4
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:30,950
Press play. The D J is fictional. But look at the card. Every line shows the exact quote, and a link to the page.

5
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:39,553
DJ Hollis Vane (fictional): They have good hoisting works and an incline.

6
00:00:40,003 --> 00:00:43,495
Quote: “They have good hoisti works and an incline”

7
00:00:43,695 --> 00:00:49,683
The quote is word for word, typos and all. A code check rejects any quote that is not in the source.

8
00:00:50,233 --> 00:00:54,704
Some hours are silent. When the archive has nothing, the D J says nothing.

9
00:00:55,254 --> 00:01:05,156
A free language model got seventy one percent of its quotes exact on the first try. After the checks, all forty claims on air are verbatim, and I read every one.

10
00:01:05,706 --> 00:01:09,276
It is open source, and the link is below. Ghost Town Radio.

